7.1.1 Bytecode File Format
--------------------------

The fcvm executes Franc C bytecode files.

   They have the following header structure:

     ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
     │ Magic Number (4 bytes)              │  0x45 0x0C 0x45 0x0C
     ├─────────────────────────────────────┤
     │ Bytecode Instructions               │  Variable length
     └─────────────────────────────────────┘

   *Magic Number*: ‘0x45 0x0C 0x45 0x0C’ (4 bytes), as defined in the
*note Franc C bytecode reference: Bytecode reference.  - Validates file
format at VM initialization - Invalid magic number triggers immediate
error


File: index.info,  Node: Command-Line Interface,  Prev: Bytecode File Format,  Up: Input Descriptions

7.1.2 Command-Line Interface
----------------------------

     ./fcvm <bytecode_file>

   *Exit Codes*:

Code      Description
----------------------------------------------------
‘0’       Success (or custom return value = 0)
‘1-255’   Custom exit code (return value mod 256)
‘84’      Any error (runtime or load-time)


