7.4.1 Undefined Behaviors
-------------------------

*Integer Overflow* - 64-bit signed integers wrap silently - Example:
‘INT64_MAX + 1’ → UNDEFINED - No error raised

   *Invalid Opcodes* - Treated as NOP (PC += 1) - Corrupted bytecode may
execute partially - No detection mechanism


File: index.info,  Node: Performance Limitations,  Next: Portability Issues,  Prev: Undefined Behaviors,  Up: Known Caveats

7.4.2 Performance Limitations
-----------------------------

*List-Based Stack* - Push/Pop: O(1) ✓ - SP-relative access: O(n) ✗ -
Impact: Slow for deep stacks (>1000 elements)

   *String Operations* - ‘AFFS’ creates intermediate structures - Linear
in string length (acceptable)


File: index.info,  Node: Portability Issues,  Prev: Performance Limitations,  Up: Known Caveats

7.4.3 Portability Issues
------------------------

*Platform Word Size* - ‘PC’ and ‘SP’ use Haskell ‘Int’ type - 32-bit
systems: Max ~2GB bytecode - 64-bit systems: Max ~8GB bytecode - Not a
practical concern for typical use

